# DTF tier manifest: npm-anon-audit  (artifact-keeper#4317, fixed by #4785, 1.11.3)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + the real npm CLI client (client.npm). The
# bug lives in repo_visibility_middleware, ahead of any storage backend, so the
# storage dimension is irrelevant.
#
# THE BUG (#4317)
# `npm audit` (and the audit step of `npm install`) POSTs the dependency tree to
#     /npm/<repo>/-/npm/v1/security/advisories/bulk   (npm >= 7)
#     /npm/<repo>/-/npm/v1/security/audits/quick      (npm 6, yarn, fallback)
# repo_visibility_middleware treats every anonymous POST as a write (#508) and
# answered 401, so an anonymous client of a PUBLIC npm repository got "Unable
# to authenticate". The permission arm also classified the POST as a write, so
# an authenticated non-admin without write got 403. The fix (#4785) adds exactly
# those two routes to both read-classified POST allowlists
# (is_anonymous_readable_format_post and is_non_mutating_format_post).
# Repository visibility is unchanged: a private repo still refuses anonymous.
#
# Oracle (oracle.sh, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX)     RED on 1.11.2: anonymous bulk + quick on a public hosted npm repo
#             and on a public remote npm repo answer 200 with the npm JSON
#             shape; a non-admin user with no write answers 200 on the public
#             repo and, with a read grant, on a private repo; a real anonymous
#             `npm audit` against the public repo exits 0.
#   (CONTROL) true on BOTH images: anonymous bulk + quick on a PRIVATE npm repo
#             are refused (401, the unauthenticated challenge); admin bulk +
#             quick work on public and private; anonymous publish (PUT) and an
#             anonymous POST one segment past the audit route stay 401; the
#             real anonymous `npm install` from the public repo succeeds.
#
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS stays at the base default (false): the remote
# repo's upstream is an unresolvable `.invalid` host, so its audit falls back
# to the handler's built-in empty report; nothing is ever fetched.
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 calls incl. Basic-auth bcrypt; keep parity with
# the other API tiers so a re-run under load never throttles a probe into a 429.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.npm"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
